# Animation Guidelines

## Framer Motion Integration
- Use Framer Motion for all animations and transitions
- Import motion components: `import { motion } from "framer-motion"`
- Add `"use client"` directive to animated components
- Use variants for consistent animation patterns

## Animation Patterns

### Container Variants
```typescript
const containerVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0 },
  visible: {
    opacity: 1,
    transition: {
      staggerChildren: 0.1, // Delay between children
      delayChildren: 0.2    // Initial delay
    }
  }
};
```

### Item Variants
```typescript
const itemVariants = {
  hidden: { y: 30, opacity: 0 },
  visible: { y: 0, opacity: 1 }
};
```

### Card Variants
```typescript
const cardVariants = {
  hidden: { scale: 0.9, opacity: 0 },
  visible: { scale: 1, opacity: 1 }
};
```

## Animation Types

### Initial Animations
- **Fade In**: `opacity: 0 → 1`
- **Slide Up**: `y: 30 → 0`
- **Scale In**: `scale: 0.8 → 1`
- **Stagger**: Use `staggerChildren` for sequential animations

### Hover Interactions
- **Scale**: `whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}`
- **Rotation**: `whileHover={{ rotate: 360 }}`
- **Elevation**: `whileHover={{ y: -5 }}`
- **Color**: Combine with CSS transitions

### Tap Interactions
- **Scale Down**: `whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}`
- **Quick Feedback**: Short duration (0.1-0.2s)

### Scroll Animations
- **In View**: `whileInView={{ opacity: 1 }}`
- **Once**: `viewport={{ once: true }}`
- **Threshold**: `viewport={{ once: true, margin: "-100px" }}`

## Animation Principles

### Performance
- Use `transform` and `opacity` properties
- Avoid animating layout properties (width, height)
- Use `will-change` CSS property when needed
- Keep animations under 60fps

### Accessibility
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Provide alternative feedback for motion-sensitive users
- Ensure animations don't cause seizures (avoid rapid flashing)

### Timing
- **Fast**: 0.1-0.3s for micro-interactions
- **Medium**: 0.4-0.6s for standard transitions
- **Slow**: 0.8-1.2s for major state changes
- Use easing functions: `ease`, `easeIn`, `easeOut`

## Component Patterns

### Animated Sections
```typescript
<motion.section
  initial={{ y: 30, opacity: 0 }}
  whileInView={{ y: 0, opacity: 1 }}
  viewport={{ once: true }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.6 }}
>
```

### Staggered Lists
```typescript
<motion.div
  variants={containerVariants}
  initial="hidden"
  whileInView="visible"
  viewport={{ once: true }}
>
  {items.map((item) => (
    <motion.div key={item.id} variants={itemVariants}>
      {/* content */}
    </motion.div>
  ))}
</motion.div>
```

### Interactive Elements
```typescript
<motion.div
  whileHover={{ scale: 1.05, y: -2 }}
  whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}
>
```

### Skills Section (Minimalist)
```typescript
// Clean, simple animations for skills
<motion.div
  whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}
  whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}
  className="text-center"
>
  <motion.div
    whileHover={{ scale: 1.05, rotate: 5 }}
    transition={{ duration: 0.3 }}
  >
    {/* Icon */}
  </motion.div>
</motion.div>
```

### Contact Section (Modern Cards)
```typescript
// Card-based contact methods
<motion.div
  whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}
  whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}
>
  <motion.a
    whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}
    whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}
  >
    {/* Contact card */}
  </motion.a>
</motion.div>
```

## Best Practices

### Consistency
- Use consistent animation durations across similar elements
- Apply same easing functions for related animations
- Maintain consistent stagger delays

### Subtlety
- Keep animations subtle and purposeful
- Avoid over-animation that distracts from content
- Use animations to guide user attention

### Loading States
- Provide animated loading indicators
- Use skeleton screens for better perceived performance
- Animate content appearance after loading

### Error Handling
- Gracefully handle animation errors
- Provide fallbacks for unsupported browsers
- Test animations across different devices